  "term": "informatics",
  "definition": "Informatics is the handling and analysis of very large, complex, and often multimodal datasets with computational and statistical methods. In mental health research, it includes working with sources such as genomics, neuroimaging, sensors, health records, administrative data, and language data to model patterns and relationships.",
